0..72 Comment "// A recursion handed through a higher-order function: `apply` takes its"
73..148 Comment "// function and its argument at one type parameter, and a call instantiates"
149..218 Comment "// that parameter at the argument\'s stage. A recursion\'s claim handed"
219..298 Comment "// on beside its predecessor takes the predecessor at that stage, one below its"
299..375 Comment "// own. `count`\'s run waits on the machine taking a type code as an argument"
376..447 Comment "// . `applyAt` is quantified over a stage instead of a type, and a call"
448..518 Comment "// instantiates the stage from its arguments; `predAt` states that its"
519..597 Comment "// result stands at its argument\'s stage, which a definition with no recursion"
598..677 Comment "// otherwise opens none for; `sameAt` takes both arguments at the stage itself,"
678..747 Comment "// which a call solves from the bound each argument shows; a call may"
748..824 Comment "// supply a stage by its binder\'s name, `applyAt[.i = j]`, which must be the"
825..894 Comment "// stage the arguments show, and so may a use passing the function as"
895..952 Comment "// a value, which stands as that call. What refuses is in"
953..1007 Comment "// `../../pathological/data/sized-higher-order.gandr`."
1008..1010 Comment "//"
1011..1025 Comment "// - see: #393"
1026..1040 Comment "// - see: #452"
1041..1055 Comment "// - see: #392"
1056..1097 Comment "// - see: #1227 — `agreed`, `appliedAt`"
1098..1128 Comment "// - see: #1498 — `passedAt`"
1129..1170 Comment "// - see: #2373 — `predAt`, `boundedAt`"
1171..1206 Comment "// - see: #1241 — `boundedHelped`"
1208..1250 Comment "// The naturals the recursion takes apart."
